Who was it, Ms. Frizzle?

00:20:33.390 --> 00:20:34.030
Uncle Shelby.

00:20:34.450 --> 00:20:37.830
Actually, Dr. Shelby, the marine biologist.

00:20:38.050 --> 00:20:40.130
He always likes to return his specimens.

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:41.730
Mert's on his way down.

00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:48.080
So long, little fella.

00:20:48.450 --> 00:20:49.670
Keep your foot out of your mouth.

00:20:55.110 --> 00:20:56.550
Welcome home, Mert.

00:20:57.020 --> 00:20:58.560
We saved your place for you.

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:04.550
Ready, class?

00:21:04.950 --> 00:21:10.180
We're going home!

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:29.820
It was a long and difficult battle.

00:21:30.160 --> 00:21:32.820
But I saved the perfect spot for us.

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:38.400
That's great, but I still don't get why you're so excited about being right here.

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:41.240
Easy. What makes a spot special?

00:21:41.540 --> 00:21:45.760
What makes a spot so good, it's worth fighting for against all odds?

00:21:46.370 --> 00:21:51.330
Well, to begin with, there has to be enough room for yourself, even if it's crowded.

00:21:51.670 --> 00:21:55.210
And you have to have the gear to handle the place you're in.

00:21:55.500 --> 00:21:57.660
And it has to be safe from danger.

00:22:01.240 --> 00:22:02.940
And to be able to breathe helps.

00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:08.640
True, all of it true, but the most important thing that makes a spot special is...

00:22:13.950 --> 00:22:17.930
And now that the ice cream truck's here, who's first in a line?

00:22:18.250 --> 00:22:29.700
Well, as I always say, picking the right place does have its reward.

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:44.960
Is this the magic school bus?

00:22:45.950 --> 00:22:47.030
Is this the magic school bus?

00:22:47.030 --> 00:22:48.290
What do you mean? Magic school bus?

00:22:49.520 --> 00:22:50.340
Magic school bus?

00:22:50.580 --> 00:22:53.000
Magic school bus?

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:14.500
Hey, Liz.

00:23:14.840 --> 00:23:17.060
Hey, come on, let's walk along the beach

00:23:17.060 --> 00:23:18.000
and see what we can find.

00:23:19.610 --> 00:23:20.530
You'll love it.

00:23:20.690 --> 00:23:21.350
Let's go.

00:23:29.100 --> 00:23:29.840
Chill out.

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:32.720
It's just the wave moving the water in and out.

00:23:33.320 --> 00:23:34.360
Oh, look at...

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:36.220
Oh, here.

00:23:36.360 --> 00:23:37.100
Could you hold on to that?

00:23:39.480 --> 00:23:39.920
Hello?

00:23:40.220 --> 00:23:41.140
Magic School Bus.

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:45.240
The things you find on the beach.

00:23:45.850 --> 00:23:49.330
Muscles and sea stars and barnacles really live in separate zones?

00:23:49.510 --> 00:23:52.190
Or were you just doing that because it made a better story?

00:23:53.020 --> 00:23:54.040
No, it's true.

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:57.240
Sometimes the zones aren't as clear as we showed.

00:23:57.600 --> 00:23:59.980
But you can still see them if you look.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:00.560
Look carefully.

00:24:04.660 --> 00:24:05.240
Thank you.

00:24:08.310 --> 00:24:12.310
These zones aren't only on rocks but on piers and pilings at the shores.

00:24:13.180 --> 00:24:18.620
Everywhere they pick places to live, according to how well they can cope with the changes of the tide.

00:24:20.120 --> 00:24:21.240
Uh, thanks for calling.

00:24:27.440 --> 00:24:29.860
Hey, Liz, you want some help with that stuff.

00:24:30.350 --> 00:24:39.620
Think you'd better leave that snail there Liz. All these plants and animals are well-suited for their particular places on the shoreline

00:24:39.620 --> 00:24:45.060
But humans and lizards can accidentally destroy their homes and their lives

00:24:45.060 --> 00:24:56.490
Better to take nothing but trash and pictures and leave behind nothing but footprints. Now. Let's go home

00:25:01.420 --> 00:25:01.600
Ha, ha, ha.

00:25:33.130 --> 00:25:36.910
There's light to the sea

00:25:36.910 --> 00:25:39.060
Come on in and don't be shy

00:25:39.060 --> 00:25:41.140
Just to make your day complete

00:25:41.140 --> 00:25:45.810
You might get back to a park inside

00:25:45.810 --> 00:25:49.460
It's a wild ride, ride
